# Code owners for se-client-kit: one code owner, a repository admin. GitHub
# requests their review on every pull request, and the `main` ruleset requires a
# code owner's approval. On a pull request the code owner authors, no one else
# can give that review, so its merge relies on the repository-admin bypass.
# The last matching pattern wins.
#
# Paths that can reach the supply chain or a credential are listed explicitly,
# even though the owners are the same as the default, so that none of them is
# left to the default silently.

*                         @mimshins

/.github/                 @mimshins
/.ai/                     @mimshins
/.claude/                 @mimshins
/.opencode/               @mimshins
/.agents/                 @mimshins
/AGENTS.md                @mimshins
/CLAUDE.md                @mimshins
/package.json             @mimshins
/pnpm-lock.yaml           @mimshins
/pnpm-workspace.yaml      @mimshins
/.npmrc                   @mimshins
/.node-version            @mimshins
/packages/contracts/      @mimshins
/specs/                   @mimshins
/decisions/               @mimshins
/runbook/                 @mimshins
/SECURITY.md              @mimshins
